    body = [=[
=2 Notes
* It is suggested that you have the three beastmen stronghold {p:Survival Guides|Survival Guide} as this quest requires traveling between the three beastmen strongholds.
* To save time, either buy an {i:Arnica Root|Arnica Root|1663} from an Auction House under Materials > {p:Alchemy} or obtain one by killing Cactuar-type mobs in {z:Eastern Altepa Desert} or {z:Western Altepa Desert}.
* Finally, bring either {i:Echo Drops|Echo Drops|4151}, {i:Holy Water|Holy Water|4154} or someone who can use {s:Cursna}.

=2 Walkthrough
* After completing {q:Missionary Moblin|Missionary Moblin|Missionary Moblin}, talk to {n:Koblakiq} at (H-11) to begin the quest.
** You will need to zone out/in after completing {q:Missionary Moblin|Missionary Moblin|Missionary Moblin} in order to initiate this quest.
* Obtain an {i:Arnica Root|Arnica Root|1663} if you haven't already.
* Head to {z:Castle Oztroja} and go to the Brass Door at (I-8). This door has two handles used to open and close the door. One handle is the opening switch and the other activates a trap door. To avoid the trap door, pull one handle, and immediately run away from the area right in front of the door. If you pull the correct switch, the door will open and you can run through safely. If you pull the wrong switch, the trap door will activate, but you should be out of the way of the trap door by then. After the trap door closes, hit the other switch and run through safely.
* On the next map, head to (G-7) and go through the exit. On the next map, this will take you to an area on a ledge. Walk along the ledge north until you see the {n:Daa Bola the Seer} at (I-7).
* Trade the {i:Arnica Root|Arnica Root|1663} to {n:Daa Bola the Seer}.
* After speaking to the yagudo, head back to {z:Oldton Movalpolos} and speak with {n:Koblakiq}.
* After receiving {@k} {k:Glittering fragment}, head to {z:Beadeaux}. Upon entering, go to (H-7) to enter the underground tunnels. From here, you can either head directly to the exit at (F-8), or you can go to the northern part of (G-7) to activate The Mute before heading to the exit at (F-8). The Mute is a device that will cast a {p:Silence} spell upon anyone who touches it. The reason these are important in Beadeaux is because there are devices called The Afflictor that will {p:curse|Curse} anyone who goes near it. These are unavoidable at many times. Your options are to either silence yourself with The Mute so that you can bypass The Afflictor unaffected, or to allow yourself to be cursed by going by The Mute while not silenced. The silence effect from The Mute can be removed by {s:Silena}, {i:Echo Drops|Echo Drops|4151} or {p:Benediction} and the curse from The Afflictor can be removed by {s:Cursna}, {i:Holy Water|Holy Water|4154}, or {p:Benediction}, although the use of Benediction in this scenario is not recommended. Also, the effects will wear off by themselves after a certain period of time.
* After going through the exit at (F-8), you will once again be above ground. Head to (E-10) to get to the upper level. You will pass The Mute and The Afflictor again on your way to (E-10). On the upper level, go to (G-10) on the large "island", where you will find {n:Ge'Fhu Yagudoeye}. Upon talking to Ge'Fhu Yagudoeye, four {p:Quadav|Category:Quadav} notorious monsters will spawn. Two of them are {m:Nickel Quadavs|Nickel Quadav}, which are {p:Paladins|Paladin}. The other two are {m:Magnes Quadavs|Magnes Quadav}, which are {p:Black Mages|Black Mage}. This fight can done solo easily by a level 75.
** Only one party member can progress this step at a time. You will have to wait 3 minutes and spawn the NMs again for each party member wanting to complete this quest.
* After the fight, talk to Ge'Fhu Yagudoeye again, and you'll receive a short cutscene. Head back to Oldton Movalpolos and speak with {n:Koblakiq} to complete the quest and receive your {i:Jaguar Mantle|Jaguar Mantle|13686} as a reward.

